{
  "description": "Identifiers of each MATLAB release: its name (R2024a), the MATLAB version that version() and VersionInfo.xml report (24.1), the MATLAB Runtime version (24.1), and the FlexLM licence version its clients check out, which lmstat prints as '(v51)'.",
  "rules": {
    "matlab": "Up to R2023a: 7.x, 8.x, 9.x with no fixed rule. From R2023b: two-digit year, then .1 for 'a' and .2 for 'b' (R2024a = 24.1).",
    "runtime": "Usually equal to the MATLAB version, but not always: R2012a = 7.17, R2015b = 9.0, R2016a = 9.0.1. Installed under a folder named 'v' plus the version digits (R2021b = 9.11 -> v911) up to R2022a, and under the release name (R2022b) from R2022b.",
    "license": "From R2007a the licence version increases by exactly 1 per release: 2*(year - 2008) + 19 + (1 if b else 0). MathWorks publishes no official table."
  },
  "caveats": [
    "The version on a licence file's INCREMENT lines (and on lmstat's '\"MATLAB\" vNN' feature header) is the newest release the licence allows, not what clients run. Only the '(vNN)' on a checkout line identifies the client.",
    "Toolboxes share MATLAB's version within a release, except discontinued or frozen products, which keep the number of their last release (e.g. Stateflow_Coder stays at 24).",
    "MathWorks uses integer versions only."
  ],
  "evidence_levels": {
    "observed": "seen side by side in a primary artefact: an installation's VersionInfo.xml, a licence file with a '# Rxxxx' header above its INCREMENT lines, an lmstat checkout from a client of a known release, or a MathWorks documentation example",
    "documented": "listed by a published table (MathWorks or an independent compilation), not checked against an artefact",
    "extrapolated": "follows from the rule; no source found"
  },
  "sources": {
    "matlab-answers-277493": "MATLAB Answers 277493, community list plus a MathWorks staff statement (MLM 35 = R2016a, 34 = R2015b): https://www.mathworks.com/matlabcentral/answers/277493-what-does-version-v35-with-lmutil-mean",
    "techoverflow-2024": "TechOverflow, 'MATLAB 20xx version to vXY version mapping' (2024-10-20): https://techoverflow.net/2024/10/20/matlab-20xx-version-to-vxy-version-mapping",
    "mathworks-doc-example": "MathWorks network licence file example ('# R2021b' header with 'INCREMENT MATLAB MLM 46'): https://www.mathworks.com/help/install/ug/network-license-files.html",
    "public-licence-files": "Public MathWorks licence files on GitHub with a '# Rxxxx' header above the INCREMENT lines, found with 'gh search code \"INCREMENT MATLAB MLM\"' (only the version field was read; cracked files with 99/369/9999 were ignored). Researched 2026-11-10.",
    "own-server": "The package author's own licence server, 2026-11-10: lmstat checkouts from an R2021a client (v45) and R2024a clients (v51); the R2026a licence file's INCREMENT lines are at 55.",
    "wikipedia-matlab": "Wikipedia, 'MATLAB', release history table (MATLAB version per release; cites MathWorks' previous-releases page): https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MATLAB#Release_history",
    "mathworks-runtime": "MathWorks, MATLAB Runtime download page, 'Release (Version)' list: https://www.mathworks.com/products/compiler/matlab-runtime.html",
    "own-installations": "The package author's own MATLAB installations, 2026-11-10: <version> in VersionInfo.xml was 9.10.0.1739362 (R2021a), 9.14.0.2239454 (R2023a), 24.1.0.2689473 (R2024a), 26.1.0.3346908 (R2026a).",
    "mathworks-runtime-folders": "MathWorks Answers 438125, 'How can I determine if MATLAB or MATLAB Runtime are installed?' (folder v911 for R2021b; release-named folders from R2022b): https://www.mathworks.com/matlabcentral/answers/438125-how-can-i-determine-if-matlab-or-matlab-runtime-are-installed"
  },
